nres has a  very special purpose in parasite which  is to create the desired audience's  emotions in every segment of the movie  in the first part we laugh at the  creativity of Kim's infiltration and we  start liking them then in the always  problematic act - it actually already  starts happening with suspense conflict  and dramatic irony and we become totally  immersed in the movie then the flood  comes and we feel sorry for the Kim's  since now we already like them thanks to  the setup in the first act and in the  final act our emotions reach a pinnacle  when we see shocking dramatic moments  immersed in meaning and you leave the  movie theater amazed of what we just saw  and then thinking about the movie for  the next couple of days this is the  effect that every screenwriter should  strive for to achieve with their readers  and their audiences I'm sure that after  the success of parasite now there will  be a lot of screenwriters trying out  this approach of mixing genres which we  definitely should try if it feels right  to you however be careful of two things  first let every genre be there for a  reason and that is to elicit certain  emotions in the audience and to  establish the pace and the structure of  the script and second if you do mix  onerous then be careful that other  screenplay elements are in unity  throughout the movie you see if you mix  onerous you cannot also mix other  elements of the screenplay because you  will create a big mess or in other words  you can break one or two screenwriting  principles but not all of them in the  same screenplay as we can learn from  parasite what it makes is yarn  the main characters in the film stay the  same the main location stays the same  and most importantly the theme of the  movie stays the same and the theme of  parasite and its clever use of the title  will be the topic of our next video so  subscribe to our channel if you don't  want to miss it also go to our patreon  page for more content where we sh